{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|# Vivida retention and monetization plan\\n2|\\n3|Last updated: 26 August 2026\\n4|\\n5|This is the implementation order for improving activation, retention, and\\n6|customer spend. It combines the repository and live-product audit with\\n7|aggregate production baselines. The order is intentional: measure the full\\n8|value and payment loop first, create a repeat-use habit second, and expand paid\\n9|inventory only after those foundations are measurable.\\n10|\\n11|## Measured baseline\\n12|\\n13|- 981 registered users; 564 MAU, 202 WAU, and 21 DAU at extraction.\\n14|- DAU / MAU is 3.7%.\\n15|- 73.7% of the measured signup cohort completed a birth profile, while 31.8%\\n16|  returned during days 1–7.\\n17|- 48.2% of MAU were active on one day only; 8.2% were active on 8+ days.\\n18|- 15,044 free credits were issued in the trailing 30 days versus 3,331 spent,\\n19|  a 4.52× supply-to-spend ratio. Purchased issuance was 140 credits across\\n20|  four users; the active-wallet median was 20 credits.\\n21|- Tarot and natal PDF reports generated 79.5% of credit consumption.\\n22|- Two users have made lifetime credit purchases and one PRO subscription was\\n23|  active at extraction. Those counts can overlap and are not summed as unique\\n24|  payers.\\n25|- Early AI chart chat and tarot usage correlate with stronger later retention,\\n26|  but both samples are small and should guide experiments rather than forecasts.\\n27|\\n28|## Priority order\\n29|\\n30|| Priority                    | Initiative                                         | Why now                                                                                                                                                                              | Success signal                                                                                 |\\n31|| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n32|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | Full value and paywall measurement                 | We can see some value actions, but not the complete exposure → selection → shortfall → checkout → unlock journey.                                                                    | Reliable value, paywall, D1/D7/D30, and payer-conversion baselines.                            |\\n33|| P0 — shipped                | Preserve calculator data through signup/onboarding | The public calculator already collects the exact birth inputs onboarding asks for again.                                                                                             | Higher calculator-to-profile completion and shorter onboarding time.                           |\\n34|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | First onboarding “aha” result                      | New users now see their personalized Big Three immediately, then receive tracked, prefilled AI question recommendations.                                                             | Higher first-value completion, recommendation click-through, and D1 return.                    |\\n35|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | Credits vs PRO comparison                          | Public natal promos, natal and first-free-tarot result states, and the Credits hub now explain one-time credits versus monthly unlimited PRO before a balance shortfall.             | Higher monetization-choice click-through and payer conversion before users reach zero credits. |\\n36|| P0 — implemented 2026-08-22 | Signup-credit cohort test                          | Future signups are assigned 50/50 to 20 credits immediately or 10 immediately plus 5 after a 24-hour return; legacy balances remain untouched.                                       | Variant-level D1/D7 retention, seven-day credit use, and 30-day payer conversion.              |\\n37|| P1 — shipped 2026-08-26     | Daily “Today” ritual                               | Daily reading, chosen focus, server-truth streak, and lifetime milestones now create a compact reason to return.                                                                     | Higher DAU/MAU, active days per MAU, and D7 retention.                                         |\\n38|| P1 — shipped 2026-08-26     | Contextual paywalls and credit-economy experiments | Shortfalls now name the deficit, compare credits with PRO, recommend the smallest sufficient pack, and return to content after verified checkout. Repeatable free earning is capped. | Higher paywall-to-checkout and 30-day payer conversion without lower retention.                |\\n39|| P1 — shipped 2026-09-05     | Reading history and journal                        | Tarot, forecasts, and AI insight do not accumulate into durable personal value.                                                     ...", "duration_ms": 73, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791096910003}
{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|# Analytics event contract (W04)\\n2|\\n3|Contract version: `v: 1` (`EVENT_CONTRACT_VERSION` in `lib/analytics.ts`).\\n4|Every product event carries `platform` (`web`), `feature`, `surface`,\\n5|`locale`, `v`. Never send user IDs, emails, names, birth data, city names,\\n6|free-text questions, or content bodies. GA4 campaign-reserved params are\\n7|stripped automatically (`stripCampaignParams`).\\n8|\\n9|## Value actions → `value_action` mirror\\n10|\\n11|These prove received value and feed the \\\"valuable sessions\\\" metric:\\n12|\\n13|| event                                                  | feature       | surface(s)                     |\\n14|| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------- | ------------------------------ |\\n15|| `compatibility_check_completed`                        | compatibility | calculator                     |\\n16|| `natal_chart_computed`                                 | natal         | calculator / onboarding result |\\n17|| `public_horoscope_read` / `daily_horoscope_read`       | horoscope     | public / dashboard             |\\n18|| `daily_ritual_completed`                               | daily         | dashboard                      |\\n19|| `tarot_reading_completed` / `tarot_followup_completed` | tarot         | tarot_reader                   |\\n20|| `ai_answer_completed`                                  | ai_chat       | chart_chat                     |\\n21|| `library_item_opened`                                  | library       | library_detail                 |\\n22|| `report_opened`                                        | report        | report_page                    |\\n23|| `relationship_insight_opened`                          | relationship  | synastry_detail (wired W12)    |\\n24|| `timing_window_opened`                                 | timing        | timing_page (wired W12)        |\\n25|| `test_completed`                                       | tests         | test surface                   |\\n26|\\n27|## Funnel / diagnostic events\\n28|\\n29|### Web app installation\\n30|\\n31|`pwa_install_cta_viewed`, `pwa_install_cta_clicked`, `pwa_install_prompt_shown`,\\n32|`pwa_install_prompt_accepted`, `pwa_install_prompt_dismissed`, and\\n33|`pwa_appinstalled` describe the browser installation path. `pwa_standalone_opened`\\n34|counts launches and `pwa_standalone_first_open` fires once per browser storage\\n35|after the installed web app opens. They carry the shared event contract and are\\n36|consent-gated. The first-open count includes earlier installs that open after\\n37|instrumentation starts, and does not reveal whether the shortcut remains on a\\n38|device. A consented first-party `/api/pwa/open` call also records a random\\n39|browser-storage profile ID in `pwa_installation`, with first and latest open\\n40|dates; the admin PWA page displays both sources separately.\\n41|\\n42|| event                                                               | when                                                                                             | key params                        |\\n43|| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\\n44|| `onboarding_started/step_viewed/step_completed/submitted/abandoned` | wizard lifecycle; abandoned = unmount without submit + last `step_name`                          | `flow`, `step_name`               |\\n45|| `search_opened/result_selected/no_result`                           | authed header people-search; no query text, `no_result` once per distinct query                  | `result_type: people`             |\\n46|| `nav_item_selected`                                                 | sidebar / drawer / tab-bar taps                                                                  | `item` (nav key)                  |\\n47|| `library_item_favorited`                                            | favorite toggle succeeds                                                                         | `outcome: favorited/unfavorited`  |\\n48|| `library_note_saved`                                                | non-empty private note saved                                                                     | `outcome: saved`                  |\\n49|| `report_downloaded`                                                 | PDF download click                                                                               | `report_type: natal`              |\\n50|| `checkout_failed`                                                   | credit top-up could not start (no URL / HTTP / network)                                          | `reason: no_url/http_NNN/network` |\\n51|| `checkout_cancel_return`                                            | Stripe `?status=canceled` return                                                                 | `outcome: canceled_at_stripe`     |\\n52|| `checko...", "duration_ms": 64, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791096910004}
{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|\\\"use client\\\";\\n2|\\n3|import { browserTrackingAllowed } from \\\"@/lib/tracking-consent\\\";\\n4|\\n5|/**\\n6| * Thin, safe wrapper over the GA4 `gtag` that @next/third-parties installs in\\n7| * production or an explicit local DebugView session (see app/layout.tsx). When\\n8| * gtag isn't loaded (normal dev / preview) this is a no-op, so call sites never have\\n9| * to guard. Use for conversion events on the public acquisition funnel\\n10| * (chart computed → email subscribed → register clicked), which — unlike raw\\n11| * bounce rate — actually tell you whether the free tools convert.\\n12| */\\n13|export type GtagParams = Record<\\n14|  string,\\n15|  string | number | boolean | null | undefined\\n16|>;\\n17|\\n18|/**\\n19| * Canonical product-event names. Keep these stable: GA4 explorations,\\n20| * audiences, and retention cohorts depend on the exact strings.\\n21| *\\n22| * Event payloads must stay aggregate and non-identifying. Never send email,\\n23| * names, user IDs, birth dates/times, city names, free-text questions, or\\n24| * profile content through this client analytics layer.\\n25| */\\n26|export const ANALYTICS_EVENT = {\\n27|  homePrimaryCtaClick: \\\"home_primary_cta_click\\\",\\n28|  compatibilityCheckCompleted: \\\"compatibility_check_completed\\\",\\n29|  compatibilityShare: \\\"compatibility_share\\\",\\n30|  natalChartComputed: \\\"natal_chart_computed\\\",\\n31|  natalChartShared: \\\"natal_chart_shared\\\",\\n32|  horoscopeEmailSubscribed: \\\"horoscope_email_subscribed\\\",\\n33|  registerClick: \\\"register_click\\\",\\n34|  signUpGoogleClick: \\\"sign_up_google_click\\\",\\n35|  signUpAppleClick: \\\"sign_up_apple_click\\\",\\n36|  signUpSubmitted: \\\"sign_up_submitted\\\",\\n37|  signUpVerified: \\\"sign_up_verified\\\",\\n38|  onboardingStarted: \\\"onboarding_started\\\",\\n39|  onboardingStepViewed: \\\"onboarding_step_viewed\\\",\\n40|  onboardingStepCompleted: \\\"onboarding_step_completed\\\",\\n41|  onboardingPrefilled: \\\"onboarding_prefilled\\\",\\n42|  onboardingSubmitted: \\\"onboarding_submitted\\\",\\n43|  publicHoroscopeRead: \\\"public_horoscope_read\\\",\\n44|  dailyHoroscopeViewed: \\\"daily_horoscope_viewed\\\",\\n45|  dailyHoroscopeRead: \\\"daily_horoscope_read\\\",\\n46|  dailyFocusSelected: \\\"daily_focus_selected\\\",\\n47|  dailyRitualCompleted: \\\"daily_ritual_completed\\\",\\n48|  pushPromptViewed: \\\"push_prompt_viewed\\\",\\n49|  pushEnabled: \\\"push_enabled\\\",\\n50|  pushDismissed: \\\"push_dismissed\\\",\\n51|  pushPermissionDenied: \\\"push_permission_denied\\\",\\n52|  tarotLoginRequired: \\\"tarot_login_required\\\",\\n53|  tarotCreditsShort: \\\"tarot_credits_short\\\",\\n54|  tarotTeaserShown: \\\"tarot_teaser_shown\\\",\\n55|  tarotReadingCompleted: \\\"tarot_reading_completed\\\",\\n56|  tarotFollowupCompleted: \\\"tarot_followup_completed\\\",\\n57|  testCompleted: \\\"test_completed\\\",\\n58|  firstResultViewed: \\\"first_result_viewed\\\",\\n59|  recommendationClicked: \\\"recommendation_clicked\\\",\\n60|  paywallViewed: \\\"paywall_viewed\\\",\\n61|  productSelected: \\\"product_selected\\\",\\n62|  insufficientCredits: \\\"insufficient_credits\\\",\\n63|  creditUnlock: \\\"credit_unlock\\\",\\n64|  proExposure: \\\"pro_exposure\\\",\\n65|  experimentAssigned: \\\"experiment_assigned\\\",\\n66|  checkoutStarted: \\\"checkout_started\\\",\\n67|  checkoutFailed: \\\"checkout_failed\\\",\\n68|  checkoutCancelReturn: \\\"checkout_cancel_return\\\",\\n69|  checkoutSuccess: \\\"checkout_success\\\",\\n70|  purchaseCompleted: \\\"purchase_completed\\\",\\n71|  entitlementActivated: \\\"entitlement_activated\\\",\\n72|  subscriptionStarted: \\\"subscription_started\\\",\\n73|  aiAnswerCompleted: \\\"ai_answer_completed\\\",\\n74|  libraryItemOpened: \\\"library_item_opened\\\",\\n75|  libraryItemFavorited: \\\"library_item_favorited\\\",\\n76|  libraryNoteSaved: \\\"library_no